rx4:{o:["It proved every tree grows faster in shade.","It suggests young trees may benefit from some protection from heat.","It showed sunlight is harmful to all plants.","It compared different species of birds.","It proved watering is unnecessary."],a:1,e:"The results suggest, but do not prove, that protection from extreme heat may help young trees.",p:"Researchers planted identical young trees in two plots. One plot received full afternoon sunlight, while the other was partly shaded by a temporary screen. After six weeks, the shaded trees had slightly larger leaves and showed less midday wilting. The researchers cautioned that the result did not prove shade was always better; the study only suggested that protection from extreme heat could help young trees."},
rx5:{o:["To reject the experiment completely.","To limit how broadly the findings should be interpreted.","To prove shade is always necessary.","To explain how the trees were planted.","To introduce a different experiment."],a:1,e:"The final sentence cautions against treating the result as proof that shade is always better.",p:"Researchers planted identical young trees in two plots. One plot received full afternoon sunlight, while the other was partly shaded by a temporary screen. After six weeks, the shaded trees had slightly larger leaves and showed less midday wilting. The researchers cautioned that the result did not prove shade was always better; the study only suggested that protection from extreme heat could help young trees."},
rx6:{o:["The experiment proves all plants need shade.","Extreme heat may have affected the trees' condition.","The researchers forgot to water the trees.","The two plots contained different species.","The screen increased the sunlight."],a:1,e:"The passage supports the cautious conclusion that extreme heat may have affected the trees.",p:"Researchers planted identical young trees in two plots. One plot received full afternoon sunlight, while the other was partly shaded by a temporary screen. After six weeks, the shaded trees had slightly larger leaves and showed less midday wilting. The researchers cautioned that the result did not prove shade was always better; the study only suggested that protection from extreme heat could help young trees."},
rx7:{o:["A broken computer","A shortage of paper","A leaking roof","A missing teacher","A noisy classroom"],a:1,e:"The students noticed that the donated books had no price labels and organised a solution.",p:"The school library was preparing for a book fair when the students noticed that hundreds of donated books had no price labels. Rather than asking the librarian to do the work alone, they divided the books into groups, created a simple pricing system and checked one another's labels. By Friday, the books were ready for sale."},
